not disabled)","pass":true,"detail":"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"},{"id":"open-graph","label":"Open Graph tags (5/6)","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"twitter-card","label":"Twitter card metadata","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"open-social","label":"Open social presence (Mastodon/Bluesky) linked","pass":false,"detail":""}],"passed":8,"total":11,"social":[],"og":{"title":"Wind Hazard and Infrastructure Performance Center (WHIP)","description":"The mission of the Wind Hazard and Infrastructure Performance Center (WHIP-C) is to enhance the resilience of buildings and other infrastructure to severe windstorms such as hurricanes and tornadoes.Windstorms have a severe effect on society by causing large numbers of fatalities and injuries and devastating damage to residential, commercial, and industrial buildings as well as power, communication, transportation, water, and other lifeline systems. Over the last 20 years, windstorms have caused more than $300 billion in insured losses in the United States alone. The total losses are estimated to be twice that number.WHIP-C develops methods and tools for preventing wind hazards from becoming disasters. Its objectives are to seek solutions to real-world problems encountered by the industry, transfer knowledge gained from fundamental research to products and intellectual properties that benefit both the industry and researchers and develop long-term strategies for enhancing the resiliency of buildings and infrastructure to wind hazards.WHIP-C members are primarily from the insurance, risk-modeling, and construction industries. The construction industry plays a key role in reducing the vulnerability of the infrastructure, while the risk-modeling industry strives to provide accurate and credible assessments of the risk. The insurance industry benefits from reduced vulnerability and better understanding of the risk, leading to more affordable insurance and more resilient and sustainable communities.","url":"/centers/wind-hazard-and-infrastructure-performance/","image":"/assets/images/twittercard.png","siteName":null,"type":"article"},"resilience":{"checks":[{"id":"pwa-https","label":"HTTPS (required for service workers)","status":"pass","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/wind-hazard-and-infrastructure-performance/","why":"HTTPS is required for service workers and most install prompts."},{"id":"pwa-manifest","label":"Web app manifest declared","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/wind-hazard-and-infrastructure-performance/","why":"A web app manifest is required for installability and controls how the app appears when launched."},{"id":"pwa-service-worker","label":"Service worker registered","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/wind-hazard-and-infrastructure-performance/","why":"A service worker is what makes offline access, caching, and background sync possible."},{"id":"pwa-theme-color","label":"Theme color declared","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/wind-hazard-and-infrastructure-performance/","why":"Theme color controls the browser chrome/status-bar color when the site is installed or bookmarked."},{"id":"pwa-apple-touch-icon","label":"Apple touch icon (iOS/bookmark icon)","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/wind-hazard-and-infrastructure-performance/","why":"iOS uses this icon for home-screen bookmarks and \"Add to Home Screen\" — without it the icon falls back to a screenshot."},{"id":"manifest-parsed","label":"Manifest fetched and parsed successfully","status":"n/a","evidence":"No manifest declared","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/wind-hazard-and-infrastructure-performance/","why":"A manifest that fails to parse cannot drive installability or launch behavior even if the link is present."},{"id":"manifest-maskable-icon","label":"Manifest declares a maskable icon","status":"n/a","evidence":"No manifest declared","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/wind-hazard-and-infrastructure-performance/","why":"A maskable icon lets the OS safely crop/mask the app icon on different device shapes without clipping content."},{"id":"sw-active","label":"Service worker is active (not just registered)","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/wind-hazard-and-infrastructure-performance/","why":"An active service worker (not just registered) is what actually intercepts requests and serves cached content."},{"id":"sw-controlling","label":"Service worker controls this page load","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/wind-hazard-and-infrastructure-performance/","why":"A controlling service worker means THIS page load is being served/intercepted, not just a future one."},{"id":"installable","label":"Meets basic installability criteria","status":"fail","evidence":"no readable web app manifest; no service worker registered","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/wind-hazard-and-infrastructure-performance/","why":"Determines whether the browser can realistically offer \"Add to Home Screen\" / install, based on manifest + service worker + HTTPS together."}],"manifest":null,"serviceWorker":{"registered":false,"active":false,"installing":false,"waiting":false,"controllingThisPage":false}}},"publicInterest":{"engine":"public-interest","checkedAt":"2026-11-16T13:02:57.479Z","a11yStatement":{"result":"pass","url":"https://www.nsf.gov/policies/accessibility","confidence":"medium","checkedAt":"2026-11-16T13:02:56.537Z"},"carbonTxt":{"result":"fail","url":null,"valid":false,"fields":{},"checkedAt":"2026-11-16T13:02:56.538Z"},"greenWebFoundation":{"result":"fail","green":false,"hostedBy":null,"url":"https://api.thegreenwebfoundation.org/greencheck/iucrc.nsf.gov","checkedAt":"2026-11-16T13:02:56.538Z"},"sitemaps":{"xml":{"found":true,"url":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/sitemap.xml"},"human":{"found":false,"url":null},"check